# riir-infer local environment — the template for `.env` (NEVER commit `.env`).
#
# ⚠ `.env` is NOT yet in this repo's .gitignore — add it before creating one.
# Copy:  cp .env.example .env
#
# riir-infer reads NO credentials or secrets: no API keys, no tokens, and no
# script sources `.env`. The CI workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml) uses no
# repository secrets. Everything below is an optional runtime / bench / debug
# knob — export it in your shell for the run that needs it.
#
# Rule for agents: values are never printed, never committed.

# ══ Tuning / bench / debug knobs (optional) ════════════════════════════════
# Derived mechanically from every env read in tracked code (Rust env::var /
# helper fns such as env_or/env_bool/env_path, shell ${X:-}, Python
# os.environ). Format:
#   # NAME=<default>    # <default note> — <first read site> (+N more files)
# "flag; unset = off" = presence/1 enables it. "default computed in code" =
# the fallback is an expression (often a model/GGUF path) — read the site.
# The `vendor` group is honoured by the vendored CubeCL crates.
# Leave everything unset unless a bench/issue doc tells you otherwise.

# ── Knobs: crates/riir-infer-clef ──
